{#
    `.. [NAME] …` — a citation, which is a footnote whose label carries a name
    rather than a number.

    The same class, because it is the same block: what a reader sees differ is
    the label, and that is content. A page that ever does need the two apart
    has the anchor — the core writes `citation-<name>` here and `footnote-<n>`
    there, so the difference is addressable without a second name for one look.

    Renamed off the core's `.citation` for the reason `footnote.html.twig`
    gives — a class on a page this system draws is a name this system defines.
#}
<div class="sds-footnote{% if node.classes %} {{ node.classesString }}{% endif %}" id="{{ node.anchor }}">
    <div class="sds-footnote__label">[{{ node.name }}]</div>
    <div class="sds-footnote__content">
        {%- for child in node.children -%}
            {{ renderNode(child) }}
        {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
</div>
